  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is Yara Ito with zip code 75284, and they want to exchange some items. First, I need to authenticate their user ID, which was found as yara_ito_8499. Now, they mentioned two main requests: exchanging hiking boots and a jigsaw puzzle.\n\nFor the hiking boots, they want a new pair with the same specs, but if that's not possible, they want size 9, leather, and waterproof. The original order might be delivered, so I need to check the order status. If it's delivered, I can use the exchange_delivered_order_items function. But I need the order ID and item IDs for the boots. Also, they need to provide a payment method for any price difference.\n\nThen, the jigsaw puzzle exchange: they want a more fancy theme with 500 pieces less but same difficulty. Again, need the order ID and item ID for the jigsaw. Check if the new item is available and same product type. Payment method for price difference here too.\n\nI should first get the user details to find their orders. Use get_user_details with user_id yara_ito_8499. Then, look into each order to find the relevant items. Once orders and items are identified, check their status. If delivered, proceed with exchange functions. Need to confirm with the user each step, list the changes, and get payment method IDs. Make sure all parameters are correct before making the tool calls.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_user_details\", \"arguments\": {\"user_id\": \"yara_ito_8499\"}}\n",
